,"kind":"tool_result","node":"run_code","payload":{"n":17,"name":"run_code","ok":true,"result":{"results":[{"candidate_id":"c156","passed":3,"total":3},{"candidate_id":"c122","passed":1,"total":3},{"candidate_id":"c049","passed":2,"total":3},{"candidate_id":"c066","passed":3,"total":3},{"candidate_id":"c002","passed":2,"total":3}]}},"seq":152,"ts":1793426174200},{"runId":"run_mvvzl4ex","kind":"llm","node":"llm","payload":{"purpose":"supervisor:ASSESS","cached":false,"costUsd":0.0033,"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","ms":1026,"usage":{"input":31984,"output":150,"cacheRead":2979,"cacheWrite":0}},"seq":153,"ts":1793426175228},{"runId":"run_mvvzl4ex","kind":"reason","node":"grade_answer","payload":{"n":18,"text":"Sandbox results are in (c156 3/3, c066 3/3, c049 2/3, c002 2/3, c122 1/3); grading the rubric against these test results.","source":"llm"},"seq":154,"ts":1793426175228},{"runId":"run_mvvzl4ex","kind":"tool_call","node":"grade_answer","payload":{"n":18,"name":"grade_answer","input":{"candidate_ids":["c156","c122","c049","c066","c002"],"regrade":false},"phase":"ASSESS"},"seq":155,"ts":1793426175228},{"runId":"run_mvvzl4ex","kind":"llm","node":"llm","payload":{"purpose":"decide:short_answer_pass","cached":false,"costUsd":0.00015,"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","ms":1321,"usage":{"input":637,"output":164,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0}},"seq":156,"ts":1793426176550},{"runId":"run_mvvzl4ex","kind":"decision","node":"decide","payload":{"task":"short_answer_pass","by":"claude","label":"yes","confidence":0.93,"costUsd":0.000146,"input":{"question":"You are adding a search endpoint to a retrieval service. Clients need to page through results and filter by metadata. In a few sentences, describe the reques…","rubric":"A good answer proposes a concrete request and response shape, such as a JSON body with query vector or text, a filter object, and a limit with an opaque curs…","answer":"I would use a POST or GET search endpoint with a typed request body: `query` (text or vector reference), `limit` (default 20, hard cap 100), `cursor` (opaque…"},"rationale":"Proposes a concrete typed request (query, limit with cap, opaque cursor rather than offset, filters object) and response shape (items with id/score/metadata, next_cursor, schema_version). Handles pagination stability via sort key plus snapshot marker, validates filters against an explicit allowlist with a 400 naming the unknown field, and keeps the API stable through additive-only changes and versioning. Covers all expected qualities."},"seq":157,"ts":1793426176550},{"runId":"run_mvvzl4ex","kind":"llm","node":"llm","payload":{"purpose":"grade","cached":false,"costUsd":0.00032,"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","ms":1926,"usage":{"input":1680,"output":305,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0}},"seq":158,"ts":1793426178477},{"runId":"run_mvvzl4ex","kind":"llm","node":"llm","payload":{"purpose":"decide:short_answer_pass","cached":false,"costUsd":0.00026,"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","ms":2313,"usage":{"input":611,"output":404,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0}},"seq":159,"ts":1793426180791},{"runId":"run_mvvzl4ex","kind":"decision","node":"decide","payload":{"task":"short_answer_pass","by":"claude","label":"yes","confidence":0.6,"costUsd":0.000263,"input":{"question":"A Postgres table stores 50 million document chunks with a 768-dimension embedding column and a tenant_id column. Queries always filter by tenant_id and then …","rubric":"A strong answer proposes a pgvector HNSW or IVFFlat index on the embedding column, and considers tenant_id through a partial index, partitioning, or a compos…","answer":"I'd add an index on the embedding column so the nearest-neighbour search doesn't scan everything. For 50 million rows, I'd probably use pgvector with an HNSW…"},"rationale":"The answer proposes pgvector HNSW for the embedding column, names a real trade-off (HNSW uses more memory and builds slower than IVFFlat but queries faster), and mentions tenant_id via a partial or btree index. The EXPLAIN ANALYZE check is generic ('look for an index scan') without naming the vector index or an expected row estimate. The tenant_id handling is vague and does not weigh the options, so the answer is shallow but meets the core expectations."},"seq":160,"ts":1793426180792},{"runId":"run_mvvzl4ex","kind":"llm","node":"llm","payload":{"purpose":"grade","cached":false,"costUsd":0.00051,"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","ms":3790,"usage":{"input":1496,"output":714,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0}},"seq":161,"ts":1793426184582},{"runId":"run_mvvzl4ex","kind":"llm","node":"llm","payload":{"purpose":"decide:short_answer_pass","cached":false,"costUsd":0.00015,"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","ms":1834,"usage":{"input":567,"output":177,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0}},"seq":162,"ts":1793426186416},{"runId":"run_mvvzl4ex","kind":"decision","node":"decide","payload":{"task":"short_answer_pass","by":"claude","label":"yes","confidence":0.92,"costUsd":0.000145,"input":{"question":"You are adding a search endpoint to a retrieval service. Clients need to page through results and filter by metadata. In a few sentences, describe the reques…","rubric":"A good answer proposes a concrete request and response shape, such as a JSON body with query vector or text, a filter object, and a limit with an opaque curs…","answer":"I'd use a POST or GET search request with a query string, a `limit` (default 20, max 100) and an opaque `cursor` for pagination, plus a `filters` object whos…"},"rationale":"Proposes a concrete request shape (query, limit with max, opaque cursor, typed filters allowlist) and a response shape (items, score, metadata, next_cursor, schema_version). Explains cursor-based pagination over sort keys to avoid offset drift, and validates filters against a versioned schema with 400 errors naming unknown fields, supporting stable evolution. Covers all expected qualities, though it is brief and does not spell out additive-only change policy in detail."},"seq":163,"ts":1793426186416},{"runId":"run_mvvzl4ex","kind":"llm","node":"llm","payload":{"purpose":"grade","cached":false,"costUsd":0.00041,"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","ms":3408,"usage":{"input":1466,"output":520,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0}},"seq":164,"ts":1793426189824},{"runId":"run_mvvzl4ex","kind":"llm","node":"llm","payload":{"purpose":"decide:short_answer_pass","cached":false,"costUsd":0.00017,"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","ms":1725,"usage":{"input":670,"output":209,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0}},"seq":165,"ts":1793426191550},{"runId":"run_mvvzl4ex","kind":"decision","node":"decide","payload":{"task":"short_answer_pass","by":"claude","label":"yes","confidence":0.92,"costUsd":0.000171,"input":{"question":"You are adding a search endpoint to a retrieval service. Clients need to page through results and filter by metadata. In a few sentences, describe the reques…","rubric":"A good answer proposes a concrete request and response shape, such as a JSON body with query vector or text, a filter object, and a limit with an opaque curs…","answer":"I would expose a GET /v1/search endpoint that takes a query string or vector reference, a filters object keyed by declared metadata fields, and a cursor plus…"},"rationale":"Proposes a concrete GET /v1/search shape with query, filters object, cursor and limit, and an results array with opaque next_cursor. Explains keyset cursors over (score, id) instead of offsets with a sound reason. Validates filters against declared fields with 400 errors listing supported fields, checks types and ranges, and adds additive-only schema evolution with versioning. Covers all expected qualities concisely. Minor gap: it does not explicitly mention the allowlist term or discuss versioning of the response beyond the /v1 prefix, but the substance is present."},"seq":166,"ts":1793426191550},{"runId":"run_mvvzl4ex","kind":"llm","node":"llm","payload":{"purpose":"grade","cached":false,"costUsd":0.00041,"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","ms":2568,"usage":{"input":1618,"output":494,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0}},"seq":167,"ts":1793426194118}