ind":"llm","node":"llm","payload":{"purpose":"supervisor:ASSESS","cached":false,"costUsd":0.00421,"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","ms":1907,"usage":{"input":40413,"output":272,"cacheRead":2979,"cacheWrite":0}},"seq":222,"ts":1793426302406},{"runId":"prewarm_0_mvvzoa7p","kind":"reason","node":"grade_answer","payload":{"n":25,"text":"Sandbox results are in for four candidates (c156 3/3, c066 3/3, c049 2/3, c002 2/3); grading their collected answers against the rubric to combine with the tests. Last call in budget.","source":"llm"},"seq":223,"ts":1793426302406},{"runId":"prewarm_0_mvvzoa7p","kind":"tool_call","node":"grade_answer","payload":{"n":25,"name":"grade_answer","input":{"candidate_ids":["c156","c049","c066","c002"],"regrade":false},"phase":"ASSESS"},"seq":224,"ts":1793426302406},{"runId":"prewarm_0_mvvzoa7p","kind":"llm","node":"llm","payload":{"purpose":"decide:short_answer_pass","cached":true,"costUsd":0,"wouldCost":0.0001457,"model":"claude-haiku-5-5"},"seq":225,"ts":1793426302407},{"runId":"prewarm_0_mvvzoa7p","kind":"decision","node":"decide","payload":{"task":"short_answer_pass","by":"claude","label":"yes","confidence":0.93,"costUsd":0,"input":{"question":"You are adding a search endpoint to a retrieval service. Clients need to page through results and filter by metadata. In a few sentences, describe the reques…","rubric":"A good answer proposes a concrete request and response shape, such as a JSON body with query vector or text, a filter object, and a limit with an opaque curs…","answer":"I would use a POST or GET search endpoint with a typed request body: `query` (text or vector reference), `limit` (default 20, hard cap 100), `cursor` (opaque…"},"rationale":"Proposes a concrete typed request (query, limit with cap, opaque cursor rather than offset, filters object) and response shape (items with id/score/metadata, next_cursor, schema_version). Handles pagination stability via sort key plus snapshot marker, validates filters against an explicit allowlist with a 400 naming the unknown field, and keeps the API stable through additive-only changes and versioning. Covers all expected qualities."},"seq":226,"ts":1793426302407},{"runId":"prewarm_0_mvvzoa7p","kind":"llm","node":"llm","payload":{"purpose":"grade","cached":true,"costUsd":0,"wouldCost":0.0003205,"model":"claude-haiku-5-5"},"seq":227,"ts":1793426302407},{"runId":"prewarm_0_mvvzoa7p","kind":"llm","node":"llm","payload":{"purpose":"decide:short_answer_pass","cached":true,"costUsd":0,"wouldCost":0.00014519999999999998,"model":"claude-haiku-5-5"},"seq":228,"ts":1793426302408},{"runId":"prewarm_0_mvvzoa7p","kind":"decision","node":"decide","payload":{"task":"short_answer_pass","by":"claude","label":"yes","confidence":0.92,"costUsd":0,"input":{"question":"You are adding a search endpoint to a retrieval service. Clients need to page through results and filter by metadata. In a few sentences, describe the reques…","rubric":"A good answer proposes a concrete request and response shape, such as a JSON body with query vector or text, a filter object, and a limit with an opaque curs…","answer":"I'd use a POST or GET search request with a query string, a `limit` (default 20, max 100) and an opaque `cursor` for pagination, plus a `filters` object whos…"},"rationale":"Proposes a concrete request shape (query, limit with max, opaque cursor, typed filters allowlist) and a response shape (items, score, metadata, next_cursor, schema_version). Explains cursor-based pagination over sort keys to avoid offset drift, and validates filters against a versioned schema with 400 errors naming unknown fields, supporting stable evolution. Covers all expected qualities, though it is brief and does not spell out additive-only change policy in detail."},"seq":229,"ts":1793426302408},{"runId":"prewarm_0_mvvzoa7p","kind":"llm","node":"llm","payload":{"purpose":"grade","cached":true,"costUsd":0,"wouldCost":0.0004066,"model":"claude-haiku-5-5"},"seq":230,"ts":1793426302408},{"runId":"prewarm_0_mvvzoa7p","kind":"llm","node":"llm","payload":{"purpose":"decide:short_answer_pass","cached":true,"costUsd":0,"wouldCost":0.0001715,"model":"claude-haiku-5-5"},"seq":231,"ts":1793426302408},{"runId":"prewarm_0_mvvzoa7p","kind":"decision","node":"decide","payload":{"task":"short_answer_pass","by":"claude","label":"yes","confidence":0.92,"costUsd":0,"input":{"question":"You are adding a search endpoint to a retrieval service. Clients need to page through results and filter by metadata. In a few sentences, describe the reques…","rubric":"A good answer proposes a concrete request and response shape, such as a JSON body with query vector or text, a filter object, and a limit with an opaque curs…","answer":"I would expose a GET /v1/search endpoint that takes a query string or vector reference, a filters object keyed by declared metadata fields, and a cursor plus…"},"rationale":"Proposes a concrete GET /v1/search shape with query, filters object, cursor and limit, and an results array with opaque next_cursor. Explains keyset cursors over (score, id) instead of offsets with a sound reason. Validates filters against declared fields with 400 errors listing supported fields, checks types and ranges, and adds additive-only schema evolution with versioning. Covers all expected qualities concisely. Minor gap: it does not explicitly mention the allowlist term or discuss versioning of the response beyond the /v1 prefix, but the substance is present."},"seq":232,"ts":1793426302408},{"runId":"prewarm_0_mvvzoa7p","kind":"llm","node":"llm","payload":{"purpose":"grade","cached":true,"costUsd":0,"wouldCost":0.0004088,"model":"claude-haiku-5-5"},"seq":233,"ts":1793426302408},{"runId":"prewarm_0_mvvzoa7p","kind":"llm","node":"llm","payload":{"purpose":"decide:short_answer_pass","cached":true,"costUsd":0,"wouldCost":0.0001823,"model":"claude-haiku-5-5"},"seq":234,"ts":1793426302408},{"runId":"prewarm_0_mvvzoa7p","kind":"decision","node":"decide","payload":{"task":"short_answer_pass","by":"claude",