in our prompt. Usually I'd rerun the held-out set and look at which cases fail. I'd also compare ou…"},{"kind":"scenario","preview":"I'd start by writing a prompt that asks the model to return the vendor, date, total, and currency as JSON. I'd include a few examples and t…"},{"kind":"code","preview":"function solve(input) {\n  const parts = input.split('---');\n  const template = parts[0];\n  const data = JSON.parse(parts[1]);\n  let out = t…"}]},{"candidate_id":"c020","answers":[{"kind":"short","preview":"I'd check whether the prompt or the model changed, then look at a few failing examples. Usually the new version formats output a bit differ…"},{"kind":"scenario","preview":"I'd write a prompt that asks the model to return only JSON with vendor, date, total, and currency keys, and give it a sample input and outp…"},{"kind":"code","preview":"function solve(input) {\n  const parts = input.split('---');\n  const template = parts[0];\n  const vals = JSON.parse(parts[1]);\n  return temp…"}]},{"candidate_id":"c100","answers":[{"kind":"short","preview":"Two likely causes are chunking that splits a policy clause across chunks, so neither chunk alone holds the answer, and weak retrieval ranki…"},{"kind":"scenario","preview":"I'd tighten the prompt by putting the schema in a system message and adding an explicit instruction to return only a JSON object with no su…"},{"kind":"code","preview":"function solve(input) {\n  const idx = input.indexOf('\\nVARS:');\n  const template = input.slice(0, idx);\n  const vars = JSON.parse(input.sli…"}]}]}},"seq":129,"ts":1793426992743},{"runId":"run_mvw030g8","kind":"llm","node":"llm","payload":{"purpose":"supervisor:ASSESS","cached":false,"costUsd":0.00378,"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","ms":1839,"usage":{"input":36925,"output":121,"cacheRead":3065,"cacheWrite":0}},"seq":130,"ts":1793426994585},{"runId":"run_mvw030g8","kind":"reason","node":"run_code","payload":{"n":20,"text":"Responses are collected for all three candidates; their JavaScript 