proposes re-running a fixed evaluation set against old and new versions, comparing outputs case by case…","answer":"I'd check what changed in the model and in our prompt. Usually I'd rerun the held-out set and look at which cases fail. I'd also compare outputs from the old…"},"rationale":"Mentions rerunning the held-out set and comparing old and new outputs, which is partly right. But it lacks specifics: no check for format or instruction-following regressions, no concrete fixes like pinning the model version or adding output validation, and no mention of version-controlling prompts. 'Adjust the eval to get it working again' suggests moving the goalposts rather than fixing the regression."},"seq":138,"ts":1793426997812},{"runId":"run_mvw030g8","kind":"llm","node":"llm","payload":{"purpose":"grade","cached":false,"costUsd":0.00043,"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","ms":3454,"usage":{"input":1246,"output":608,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0}},"seq":139,"ts":1793427001266},{"runId":"run_mvw030g8","kind":"llm","node":"llm","payload":{"purpose":"decide:short_answer_pass","cached":false,"costUsd":0.0002,"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","ms":2122,"usage":{"input":435,"output":313,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0}},"seq":140,"ts":1793427003389},{"runId":"run_mvw030g8","kind":"decision","node":"decide","payload":{"task":"short_answer_pass","by":"claude","label":"no","confidence":0.8,"costUsd":0.0002,"input":{"question":"A prompt that works well on your test set starts failing after a model version upgrade. Describe how you would find out what changed and what you would do ab…","rubric":"A good answer separates the prompt from the model: it proposes re-running a fixed evaluation set against old and new versions, comparing outputs case by case…","answer":"I'd check whether the prompt or the model changed, then look at a few failing examples. Usually the new version formats output a bit differently or follows i…"},"rationale":"The answer separates prompt from model only loosely and proposes rerunning the test set, but it doesn't describe a fixed evaluation comparing old and new model versions case by case. It also omits concrete fixes such as pinning the model version or adding output validation, and never mentions version control for prompts. It stays vague where the question asks for a specific approach."},"seq":141,"ts":1793427003390},{"runId":"run_mvw030g8","kind":"llm","node":"llm","payload":{"purpose":"grade","cached":false,"costUsd":0.00044,"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","ms":3659,"usage":{"input":1179,"output":645,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0}},"seq":142,"ts":1793427007049},{"runId":"run_mvw030g8","kind":"llm","node":"llm","payload":{"purpose":"decide:short_answer_pass","cached":false,"costUsd":0.00012,"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","ms":1154,"usage":{"input":563,"output":132,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0}},"seq":143,"ts":1793427008203},{"runId":"run_mvw030g8","kind":"decision","node":"decide","payload":{"task":"short_answer_pass","by":"claude","label":"yes","confidence":0.9,"costUsd":0.000122,"input":{"question":"A retrieval-augmented chatbot answers questions about internal policy documents. Users report that answers are sometimes confidently wrong even though the co…","rubric":"A good answer names specific failure modes such as chunks split mid-sentence or losing their heading context, embedding mismatch between query and document p…","answer":"Two likely causes are chunking that splits a policy clause across chunks, so neither chunk alone holds the answer, and weak retrieval ranking, where the embe…"},"rationale":"The answer names two specific, plausible causes (clause split across chunks, weak ranking favoring semantically similar but wrong sections) and pairs each with a concrete fix (overlapping chunks with headers retained; hybrid BM25 plus embedding search with cross-encoder reranking). It matches the expected qualities and is concise."},"seq":144,"ts":1793427008203},{"runId":"run_mvw030g8","kind":"llm","node":"llm","payload":{"purpose":"grade","cached":false,"costUsd":0.00051,"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","ms":3797,"usage":{"input":1547,"output":720,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0}},"seq":145,"ts":1793427012000},{"runId":"run_mvw030g8","kind":"tool_result","node":"grade_answer","payload":{"n":21,"name":"grade_answer","ok":true,"result":{"graded":3,"results":[{"candidate_id":"c077","total":0.3,"parts":[{"kind":"short","score":0.3,"confidence":0.8},{"kind":"scenario","score":0.25,"confidence":0.8},{"kind":"code","score":0.35,"confidence":0.85}]},{"candidate_id":"c020","total":0.25,"parts":[{"kind":"short","score":0.3,"confidence":0.8},{"kind":"scenario","score":0.1,"confidence":0.85},{"kind":"code","score":0.35,"confidence":0.8}]},{"candidate_id":"c100","total":0.633,"parts":[{"kind":"short","score":0.9,"confidence":0.85},{"kind":"scenario","score":0.7,"confidence":0.75},{"kind":"code","score":0.3,"confidence":0.85}]}]}},"seq":146,"ts":1793427012000},{"runId":"run_mvw030g8","kind":"llm","node":"llm","payload":{"purpose":"supervisor:ASSESS","cached":false,"costUsd":0.00417,"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","ms":2025,"usage":{"input":39850,"output":316,"cacheRead":3065,"cacheWrite":0}},"seq":147,"ts":1793427014028},{"runId":"run_mvw030g8","kind":"reason","node":"advance_phase","payload":{"n":22,"text":"All three approved candidates are assessed, graded, and unflagged (c100 0.63, c077 0.30, c020 0.25), so the ASSESS exit condition holds.","source":"llm"},"seq":148,"ts":1793427014029},{"runId":"run_mvw030g8","kind":"tool_call","node":"advance_phase","payload":{"n":22,"name":"advance_phase","input":{},"phase":"ASSESS"},"seq":149,"ts":1793427014029},{"runId":"run_mvw030g8","kind":"tool_result","node":"advance_phase","payload":{"n":22,"name":"advance_phase","ok":true,"result":{"phase":"AUDIT","exitCondition":"fairness_audit has run on the current live shortlist"}},"seq":150,"ts":1793427014029},{"runId":"run_mvw030g8","kind":"llm","node":"llm","payload":{"purpose":"supervisor:AUDIT","cached":false,"costUsd":0.00421,"model":"claude-h