aluation work described. Assessment: all three passed 2 of 3 sandbox code tests; rubric grades are unflagged. Fairness audit: Spearman 0.5, top-5 overlap 100%, no candidate moved 3 or more places, so blind ranking is not recommended. The pool was thin on real LLM-app evaluation work, so HR may want to widen sourcing to reach five.","official_blind":false},"phase":"FINALIZE"},"seq":166,"ts":1793427026033},{"runId":"run_mvw030g8","kind":"tool_result","node":"finalize_shortlist","payload":{"n":26,"name":"finalize_shortlist","ok":true,"result":{"done":true,"ranked":["c100","c077","c020"]}},"seq":167,"ts":1793427026033},{"runId":"run_mvw030g8","kind":"done","node":"finalize_shortlist","payload":{"final":{"ranked":["c100","c077","c020"],"weights":{"semantic":0.6,"assessment":0.4},"summary":"Shortlist has 3 of the 5 targeted candidates, all with verbatim evidence for both must-haves (LLM applications, evaluation). Final scores (0.6 semantic + 0.4 assessment): c100 Ravi Bose 0.648 (semantic 0.66, rubric grade 0.63); c077 Ivan Petrov 0.528 (semantic 0.68, grade 0.30); c020 Nora Sharma 0.49 (semantic 0.65, grade 0.25). Tool calls: 25 of 25 used. Reformulations: 1 of 2 (the shipped-work wording for LLM applications). Dropped: c060 Ravi Sharma and c131 Rahul Bose, both keyword-only profiles whose citations failed for both must-haves, with no build or evaluation work described. Assessment: all three passed 2 of 3 sandbox code tests; rubric grades are unflagged. Fairness audit: Spearman 0.5, top-5 overlap 100%, no candidate moved 3 or more places, so blind ranking is not recommended. The pool was thin on real LLM-app evaluation work, so HR may want to widen sourcing to reach five.","officialBlind":false},"summary":{"toolCalls":26,"reformulations":1,"dropped":[{"id":"c060","name":"Ravi Sharma","reason":"Keyword-only skill claims for both must-haves; profile shows game development, no LLM build or evaluation work."},{"id":"c131","name":"Rahul Bose","reason":"m1 and m2 supported onl