didate_id":"c122","answers":[{"kind":"short","preview":"I'd add a B-tree index on tenant_id so the tenant filter narrows rows first, and an HNSW index on the embedding column using vector_cosine_…"},{"kind":"scenario","preview":"I'd make POST /v1/searches take a JSON body with query, filters, and page_size, and return a results array plus a next_cursor string. For p…"},{"kind":"code","preview":"function solve(input) {\n  if (!input) return input;\n  const pairs = input.split('&');\n  pairs.sort();\n  return pairs.join('&');\n}"}]},{"candidate_id":"c002","answers":[{"kind":"short","preview":"Reference answer (not a candidate response): Use a POST /search request with a JSON body containing query, a limit capped at 100, an opaque…"},{"kind":"scenario","preview":"Reference answer (not a candidate response): Add the new field name alongside the old one and emit both for a deprecation window. Publish t…"},{"kind":"code","preview":"function solve(input) {\n  let queries;\n  try {\n    queries = JSON.parse(input);\n  } catch (e) {\n    throw new Error(\"input is not valid JSO…"}]}]}},"seq":155,"ts":1793427253270},{"runId":"run_mvw09e3zybn","kind":"llm","node":"llm","payload":{"purpose":"supervisor:ASSESS","cached":false,"costUsd":0.00309,"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","ms":1027,"usage":{"input":29926,"output":133,"cacheRead":3065,"cacheWrite":0}},"seq":156,"ts":1793427254300},{"runId":"run_mvw09e3zybn","kind":"reason","node":"run_code","payload":{"n":16,"text":"Responses are collected for all five approved candidates, and their JavaScript code answers need to be run against the hidden tests before grading.","source":"llm"},"seq":157,"ts":1793427254300},{"runId":"run_mvw09e3zybn","kind":"tool_call","node":"run_code","payload":{"n":16,"name":"run_code","input":{"candidate_ids":["c049","c156","c066","c122","c002"]},"phase":"ASSESS"},"seq":158,"ts":1793427254300},{"runId":"run_mvw09e3zybn","kind":"tool_result","node":"run_code","payload":{"n":16,"name":"run_code","ok":false,"error":"a is not a function"},"seq":159,"ts":1793427254307},{"runId":"run_mvw09e3zybn","kind":"llm","node":"llm","payload":{"purpose":"supervisor:ASSESS","cached":false,"costUsd":0.00326,"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","ms":1926,"usage":{"input":31090,"output":242,"cacheRead":3065,"cacheWrite":0}},"seq":160,"ts":1793427256235},{"runId":"run_mvw09e3zybn","kind":"reason","node":"run_code","payload":{"n":17,"text":"The first run_code call errored in the sandbox harness (\"a is not a function\") before any candidate code could be tested, so I'm retrying the same five candidates once.","source":"llm"},"seq":161,"ts":1793427256236},{"runId":"run_mvw09e3zybn","kind":"tool_call","node":"run_code","payload":{"n":17,"name":"run_code","input":{"candidate_ids":["c049","c156","c066","c122","c002"]},"phase":"ASSESS"},"seq":162,"ts":1793427256236},{"runId":"run_mvw09e3zybn","kind":"tool_result","node":"run_code","payload":{"n":17,"name":"run_code","ok":false,"error":"a is not a function"},"seq":163,"ts":1793427256236},{"runId":"run_mvw09e3zybn","kind":"llm","node":"llm","payload":{"purpose":"supervisor:ASSESS","cached":false,"costUsd":0.00345,"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","ms":2421,"usage":{"input":32310,"output":382,"cacheRead":3065,"cacheWrite":0}},"seq":164,"ts":1793427258660},{"runId":"run_mvw09e3zybn","kind":"reason","node":"grade_answer","payload":{"n":18,"text":"run_code has failed twice with a sandbox harness error (\"a is not a function\"), so the rubric grade will rest on the collected answers alone and any test-based disagreement will need to be flagged.","source":"llm"},"seq":165,"ts":1793427258660},{"runId":"run_mvw09e3zybn","kind":"tool_call","node":"grade_answer","payload":{"n":18,"name":"grade_answer","input":{"candidate_ids":["c049","c156","c066","c122","c002"],"regrade":false},"phase":"ASSESS"},"seq":166,"ts":1793427258661},{"runId":"run_mvw09e3zybn","kind":"llm","node":"llm","payload":{"purpose":"decide:short_answer_pass","cached":true,"costUsd":0,"wouldCost":0.0001256,"model":"claude-haiku-5-5"},"seq":167,"ts":1793427258662},{"runId":"run_mvw09e3zybn","kind":"decision","node":"decide","payload":{"task":"short_answer_pass","by":"claude","label":"yes","confidence":0.9,"costUsd":0,"input":{"question":"You are adding a search endpoint to a retrieval service. Clients need to page through results and filter by metadata. In a few sentences, describe the reques…","rubric":"A good answer proposes a concrete request and response shape, such as a JSON body with query vector or text, a filter object, and a limit with an opaque curs…","answer":"I'd expose a POST /search endpoint with a JSON body containing query_vector or query_text, a filters object validated against a versioned Pydantic model, and…"},"rationale":"Proposes a concrete POST /search request with query vector or text, a filters object, limit plus opaque cursor (not offset paging), a response with results and next_cursor, 422 on unknown filter keys (allowlist-style validation), and additive, versioned schema changes for stability. Covers all expected qualities, though brief on error detail and cursor encoding specifics."},"seq":168,"ts":1793427258663},{"runId":"run_mvw09e3zybn","kind":"llm","node":"llm","payload":{"purpose":"grade","cached":false,"costUsd":0.00038,"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","ms":2876,"usage":{"input":1367,"output":493,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0}},"seq":169,"ts":1793427261541},{"runId":"run_mvw09e3zybn","kind":"llm","node":"llm","payload":{"purpose":"decide:short_answer_pass","cached":true,"costUsd":0,"wouldCost":0.0001341,"model":"claude-haiku-5-5"},"seq":170,"ts":1793427261541},{"runId":"run_mvw09e3zybn","kind":"decision","node":"decide","payload":{"task":"short_answer_pass","by":"claude","label":"yes","confidence":0.93,"costUsd":0,"input":{"question":"You are adding a search endpoint to a retrieval service. Clients need to page through results and filter by metadata. In a few sentences, describe the reques…","rubric":"A good answer proposes a concrete request and response shape, such as a JSON body with query vector or text, a filter object, and a limit with an opaque curs…","answer":"I would use a POST /v1/search request with a JSON body containing query (a string or vector reference), a filters object validated by a versioned Pydantic mo…"},"rationale":"Proposes a concrete request shape (POST /v1/search with query, filters, page with limit and opaque cursor), a response with results, next_cursor, and schema_version, and explicitly avoids offset paging. Covers filter validation against an allowlist with clear rejection of unknown fields, and stability via versioning and additive optional fields. Meets all expected qualities concisely."},"seq":171,"ts":1793427261542},{"runId":"run_mvw09e3zybn","kind":"llm","node":"llm","payload":{"purpose":"grade","cached":false,"costUsd":0.00047,"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","ms":3917,"usage":{"input":1572,"output":631,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0}},"seq":172,"ts":1793427265459},{"runId":"run_mvw09e3zybn","kind":"llm","node":"llm","payload":{"purpose":"decide:short_answer_pass","cached":true,"costUsd":0,"wouldCost":0.00011559999999999999,"model":"claude-haiku-5-5"},"seq":173,"ts":1793427265460},{"runId":"run_mvw09e3zybn","kind":"decision","node":"decide","payload":{"task":"short_answer_pass","by":"claude","label":"yes","confidence":0.9,"costUsd":0,"input":{"question":"In two or three sentences, describe how you would keep an embeddings pipeline correct when the embedding model is upgraded and the stored vectors must change…","rubric":"A strong answer names a versioning scheme for embeddings (model id and version stored with each vector), a backfill strategy that runs in batches without blo…","answer":"I would version every stored vector with its model identifier and keep the old and new embeddings in separate columns or tables, so nothing is overwritten mi…"},"rationale":"Covers all three expected qualities: stores model id and version with each vector, backfills in resumable id-ordered batches, and cuts over by building a parallel index and switching reads after validation, with per-request pinning to prevent mixed-model results. It is concise and within the requested length, though it does not explicitly address partial failure beyond resumability."},"seq":174,"ts":1793427265460},{"runId":"run_mvw09e3zybn","kind":"llm","node":"llm","payload":{"purpose":"grade","cached":false,"costUsd":0.00058,"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","ms":4460,"usage":{"input":1716,"output":825,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0}},"seq":175,"ts":1793427269922},{"runId":"run_mvw09e3zybn","kind":"llm","node":"llm","payload":{"purpose":"decide:short_answer_pass","cached":true,"costUsd":0,"wouldCost":0.0001996,"model":"claude-haiku-5-5"},"seq":176,"ts":1793427269922},{"runId":"run_mvw09e3zybn","kind":"decision","node":"decide","payload":{"task":"short_answer_pass","by":"claude","label":"yes","confidence":0.72,"costUsd":0,"input":{"question":"A table of 50 million document chunks stores embeddings in Postgres with pgvector. Queries filter by tenant_id and sort by cosine distance. Describe the inde…","rubric":"A strong answer names a concrete index type, such as an HNSW or IVFFlat index for the vector column, and a B-tree index on tenant_id, and it explains that a …","answer":"I'd add a B-tree index on tenant_id so the tenant filter narrows rows first, and an HNSW index on the embedding column using vector_cosine_ops so the sort ca…"},"rationale":"The answer names a concrete index for each part: a B-tree on tenant_id and an HNSW index using vector_cosine_ops. It also names ef_search as the tuning knob and correctly describes its recall-versus-latency trade-off. It omits the expected point that combining a tenant filter with an approximate index can reduce recall unless the query plan is checked, and it does not name a specific test metric. Those gaps keep it from being a strong answer, but the core requirements are met."},"seq":177,"ts":1793427269923},{"runId":"run_mvw09e3zybn","kind":"llm","nod