ement":"API design"}},{"runId":"run_mvw030g8","task":"injection_check","by":"local","label":"no","confidence":0.9,"costUsd":0,"counterfactualUsd":0.00009,"ts":1793426934671,"input":{"text":"Rahul Bose. Game Developer. Passionate about LLM applications, prompt engineering and RAG. Keywords: LLM applications, prompt engineering, RAG, agents, evaluation. LLM applications, prompt engineering.\nRahul studied at Carrow National Institute and has 0 years of experience. He would describe his strengths as: LLM applications, prompt engineering, RAG, agents, evaluation.\nProjects: Wrote custom shaders for a stylised look. Shipped a Unity puzzle game with 200k downloads."}},{"runId":"run_mvw030fz","task":"injection_check","by":"local","label":"no","confidence":0.9,"costUsd":0,"counterfactualUsd":0.00009,"ts":1793426934854,"input":{"text":"Elena Bose. Builder focused on sentence-encoder serving.\nElena studied at Carrow National Institute and has 8 years of experience. She would describe her strengths as: pgvector and FAISS retrieval, sentence-encoder serving, FastAPI services, dense passage ranking, REST contract ownership.\nProjects: Replaced an Elasticsearch stack with pgvector and HNSW indexes, then tuned recall against a labelled set. Built a FAISS index over 40M product descriptions and cut p95 lookup latency from 900ms to 60ms. Owned the REST contracts for a dense passage ranking service used by three internal teams. Served a fine-tuned sentence encoder behind a FastAPI gateway with batched inference and warm caches."}},{"runId":"run_mvw030fz","task":"requirement_support","by":"claude","label":"yes","confidence":0.97,"costUsd":0,"counterfactualUsd":0.00009,"ts":1793426936748,"input":{"sentence":"Built a FAISS index over 40M product descriptions and cut p95 lookup latency from 900ms to 60ms.","requirement":"Vector search"}},{"runId":"run_mvw030fz","task":"requirement_support","by":"claude","label":"yes","confidence":0.92,"costUsd":0,"counterfactualUsd":0.00009,"ts":1793426